  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the differences between outcomes and a reference value (set at 500€ due to the sure outcome in B), computing the mean of these differences weighted by probabilities, and preferring the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., higher) mean difference. In this case, both lotteries have a mean difference of 0, so the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention any such calculation or consideration of deviations from the reference value. Instead, the justification is based solely on the certainty of the outcome. The individual does not reference differences, mean differences, or any evaluation of deviations. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process. The reported reasoning is inconsistent with the required elements of the decision reason (e.g., reference value, differences, mean differences).",
