  "step_2": "The individual's verbal report states: 'B mit 50% Wahrscheinlichkeit nichts zu verlieren, war lukrativer.' This translates to: 'B, with 50% probability of losing nothing, was more profitable.' The individual focuses on the 50% chance of not losing anything (i.e., receiving 0 Euros) in Lottery B, and interprets this as being more beneficial or 'lukrative' (profitable). The individual does not mention the reference value, mean differences, or any calculation involving probabilities of differences from a sure outcome. The reasoning is based solely on the prospect of avoiding a loss (i.e., not losing anything) rather than on a formal comparison of mean differences from a reference point. The individual does not consider the outcome of -1000 Euros or the full probabilistic structure of the differences from the reference value (-500). The justification is emotional or heuristic — focusing on the positive outcome (no loss) rather than a quantitative evaluation of expected value or mean differences from a reference point.",
